#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# is_lower_triangular_matrix

#% text
# `is_lower_triangular_matrix(m)` is true when every entry of `m` above the main diagonal is zero; `is_lower_triangular_matrix(m, k)` when every entry above the `k`-th diagonal is.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The result is false for anything that is not a matrix.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
is_lower_triangular_matrix([[1, 0], [2, 3]])
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_lower_triangular_matrix([[1, 2], [0, 3]])
#% output
#= false

#% cell
is_lower_triangular_matrix([[1, 2], [0, 3]], 1)
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `is_upper_triangular_matrix`, `is_diagonal_matrix`, `lower_triangularize`
